I think pets have really taken a bum rap on this newsgroup, so here
are a few words in their defense.  They can be very useful even when
you're powerful.  How many times have lost a powerful character
because he stepped on a sleeping gas trap or drank a potion of
paralysis and was hacked to pieces by a wimpy lizard or a rat?
Also, have you ever tried polymorphing your pet?  I recently
polymorphed my cat into a nalfeshnee, and it saved my ass several
times since...it even killed a shopkeeper for me.  Now that character,
which would have surely died on several occasions if not for his pet
is *very* close to hell.  Unfortunately, the nalfeshnee is dead  :( :(
It was killed by a lurker above.
   BTW, this seems like a bug to me.  The lurker above swallowed the
nalfeshnee and and killed it in just one turn.  The nalfeshnee hadn't
been in any fierce battles for a while, so it couldn't have been that
weak.  I don't get how a lurker above can kill a powerful demon so
quickly.  So my question is:  when one monster swallowed by another,
does the swallowed monster get to fight its way out or does it die
automatically?  If the latter is the case, I think it's a bug, and
should be fixed in 3.1.

